title: resourcegameBad
---
........ //for some reason this node starts on line 2
<<cs 1 4>>
<<MC true>>
{$playerName}: “It was terrible, I fucked it up. I don’t know why it went so bad, but I should’ve—”
{$mentorName}: “Calm down, rookie. Just take a breather, and tell me slowly. Did anything dangerous happen with the Pleiotium?”
{$playerName}: “No…nothing dangerous.”
{$mentorName}: “Then it’s fine. Learn from this mistake, and apply yourself to be better next time. We will return to correct this, but it will require some overtime. Everything will be okay.”
The departure from the mines consisted of only silence. Led back to a hut reserved for visiting blacksmiths, you go to sleep early on the verge of tears, swearing you will do better the next time. 
The work after was harsh, but ultimately better than your initial try. Your return to the capital was delayed due to the overtime, leaving Isham bitter on the ride back about the work he had missed.
You couldn’t help but wonder how open your schedule would have been if you had done it right the first time.
<<MC false>>
<<set $weekOneResult = 0>>
<<jump WeekTwoInteractions>>
