title: WeekTwoInteractions
---
<<change_background "map">>
Returning to the guild, you drop off the Pleiotium you harvested at your forge and retire for the weekend. 
You remember that Maeve had invited you for lunch once you were free. 
<<if $rejectedLunch == true>>
You had once turned down her offer, but it may still be possible to reconcile this old bond. 
Do you wish to make up with Maeve?
-> Yes 
    Wanting to catch up with an old friend, you let Maeve know your availability in advance. 
    <<change_background "restaurant">>
    Departing upon hearing her response, you head to the address given after cleaning yourself up from the mines.
    The restaurant was a humble store with casual dining options, providing a nice, cozy atmosphere for customers. 
    <<sp 3>>
    You see Maeve seated at a table for two, beckoning you to come with a waving hand. Taking your seat, you notice Maeve smiling at you, no uneasiness on her face as there was before.
    <<cs 3 1>>
    {$bestFriendName}: “Thank you for coming. I know you’ve been busy, but I wanted to tell you about our folks back from the village.”
    <<MC true>>
    {$playerName}: “Oh, how’s everyone been? I haven’t seen them in a while since I came to the capital.”
    <<MC false>>
    <<cs 3 0>>
    {$bestFriendName}:“Your parents are doing well. They actually asked me to find out if you managed to become an apprentice when I told them I was going to the capital next.”
    <<MC true>>
    {$playerName}: “I would appreciate it if you ever stop by there again to tell them I’m doing well for myself here and that I miss them dearly. I still can’t believe the village hasn’t managed to establish a proper route yet for mailing.”
    <<MC false>>
    {$bestFriendName}: “Our backwater home will rather watch all their children leave than even try to get with the times. That old man, Otto, still complains about how the new generations are spoiled, not having to fear being attacked on the roads by monsters like they did in the past.”
    Laughing over Maeve’s story, the two of you reminisce over the past over a delightful lunch.  
    <<cs 3 4>>
    {$bestFriendName}: “...wow, so you’re telling me you even have to do the mining yourself?”    
    <<cs 3 0>>
    {$playerName}: “It’s grueling, but rewarding work. I can’t wait to get started with smelting it.”
    {$bestFriendName}: “It’s nice that you’ve been enjoying your work. I wish I could say I’ve been the same with the knight order.”
    {$playerName}: “I’ve been meaning to ask about that, actually. You seem to have something upsetting you.”
    {$bestFriendName}: “It’s just…you ever have that experience where you finally are where you want to be, but as time passes, you start to doubt if you really belong?”
    <<MC true>>
    -> “No, I’m sorry, I can’t say for sure that I have.”
        {$bestFriendName}: “Sorry, I didn’t mean to spring that up on you. There’s been a lot on my mind lately.”
        {$playerName}: “No, it’s okay, Maeve. I’ll always be here to listen to your troubles.”
        {$bestFriendName}: “Thank you, {$playerName}. We should meet again. This was fun.” 
        After finishing lunch, the two of you depart after paying the check and saying goodbye, promising to see each other sometime in the future.
    -> “All the time, it’s something I struggle to overcome time and time again. I find that thinking back to why I came here and what I want out of myself is what helps me the most.”
        <<set $bestFriendAffinity = $bestFriendAffinity + 1>>
