-> Maeve
    <<set $bestFriendAffinity = $bestFriendAffinity + 1>>
    <<change_background "market">>
    You decide that you wish to pay Maeve a visit at her home. Finding it rude to intrude without a gift, you stop by the market first to find something for Maeve. 
    Remembering her love of sweet food, you decide to check out one of the dessert stalls. 
    The trip was short, and a delicious small chocolate cake was now boxed and ready to be gifted. 
    But as you begin to depart from the central market, you notice a peculiar piece of jewelry in the corner of your eye at a stall. Something about it draws your attention.
    -> You got your cake already, no need for more.
    -> Wouldn’t hurt to look. Why not check it out?
        Unable to resist your curiosity, you decide to check out the stand selling the piece of jewelry. 
        What you see, however, leaves you confused. It was an odd, obsidian black bracelet with not even a single engraving. There was nothing special about it, no shimmer, no luster. There was no reason for you to have been drawn to this. Yet somehow, you knew that this bracelet would fit perfectly onto Maeve.  
        You would have bought it on the spot if it weren’t for the exorbitant price it was listed at. No matter how you pleaded, the merchant would not relent. Not even accepting barter or a loan, there was nothing you could do to obtain the bracelet.
        Just why do you not have the money to afford a gift like this? If only you had more gold, more power, this would have never happened. A feeling of resentment lingers within you. 
        Perhaps it is time to leave. It would be better if this were forgotten. 
