    <<MC false>>
    <<endif>>
    <<cs 1 0>>
    Isham shakes his head, looking distant as he thinks of what to say.
    {$mentorName}: “That blueprint holds the schematic I made of a warhammer I promised to give to Silas’s father. He had been a mentor to me when I was only an apprentice, despite him being a Hunter.”
    <<cs 1 7>>
    {$mentorName}: “However, I was unable to develop the weapon in time for the man before his death. Killed by an Iron Monster alongside Silas’s mother, the poor kid was left orphaned in their early teens.”
    <<cs 1 0>>
    {$mentorName}: “Now all I want to do is perfect it, make it so powerful that no monster will stand a chance against it.”
    {$mentorName}: “Yet I am lacking. I am unable to channel what is needed to make the weapon work properly, so all I can do is redesign it over and over until it will work…a fool’s dream.”
    <<cs 1 6>>
    {$mentorName}: “...aye, that’s enough now. You heard enough of my story.”
    Unable to hold your stares of admiration, Isham looks away with his ears red in embarrassment.
    <<MC true>>
    {$playerName}: “There’s no need to be embarrassed, senior. I totally respect your dream!”
    <<MC false>>
    {$mentorName}: “Just…go. It’s the weekend, why are you still here?”
    <<MC true>>
    {$playerName}: “To see you, master!”
    <<MC false>>
    <<cs 1 6>>
    {$mentorName}: “I told you, rookie, don’t call me. You make me sound ancient.”
    Laughing over the banter between mentor and student, your bond with Isham grows. That night in the guild was filled with giggling joy until finally the two of you stopped cracking jokes with each other and left to go home.
