<<MC false>>
{$redFlagName}: “Fine, fine, I just wanted to know.”
<<MC true>>
<<cs 0 0>>
{$playerName}: “How come you are here?”
<<MC false>>
{$redFlagName}: “So demanding. You’re overthinking again, dear. I’m only here with the hopes to further explain the importance of the morningstar I wish to be made by you. Would you mind taking a seat with me here while I explain?”
Sitting down next to Judith in a corner of the commissions room, you notice she moves her chair closer to you to be by your side.
<<cs 2 2>>
{$redFlagName}: “This morningstar…is meant to serve as a memento of my late father. He passed away serving the kingdom as a Knight and I hoped to honor him with his weapon. But I never managed to find it after the Iron Crusade. It was lost along with his body.”
<<cs 2 0>>
{$redFlagName}: “That’s why I am hoping to rebuild it. It won’t be the real thing, sure, but I can remember enough about his weapon from my childhood to create a blueprint similar to it. That way, I can still remember his face when I grow old. But for that to happen, I need a blacksmith capable enough to recreate it, and that’s when I found you.”
{$redFlagName}: “So…what do you say? Think you can be that blacksmith for me? Help me, and I'll help you. Wouldn’t you want that type of relationship with me?”
Judith leans closer to you, placing her hand onto yours. You look into her crimson eyes, unsure of her intentions. She is inviting you…but to what?
<<MC true>>
-> Lean in, close your eyes, and let her guide you.
    <<set $redFlagAffinity = $redFlagAffinity + 2>>
    <<cs 0 4>>
    No words were spoken. You feel her soft, warm lips connect with yours, tenacious with vigor, as if she would not let you go now that she finally has you. You drown in the sensation of passion, your mind a fog, and your heart aflame. 
    Did you finally lose your mind? A relationship like this with a customer? You could be fired, your dream shattered. She could be using you, hoping to leave you ruined by the end. 
    You pull back, confused about how weak-minded you are. Will she protect you if something were to happen? Is this something you wish to continue? 
    But when you look back at her and see her smile, you realize it no longer matters. The deed is done.
    The consequences will arrive no matter what you do, but at the very least, you can decide how this path will go. You just need time to sort your emotions.
    {$playerName}: “I think I need some time alone to think, Lady Sinclair. I’m sorry, I have to go.” 
    Before she can say anything else, you leave the room in haste, back to your forge.
