Before she can say anything else, you leave the room in haste, back to your forge.
<<change_background "personal forge">>
Hunched over your anvil, you cradle your head as your brain races through a chaotic stream of thoughts. 
Your relationship with Judith is bound to change, depending on what you choose. 
As you are contemplating, however, you notice a piece of paper slip through the bottom opening of your door. 
Snapped out of your thoughts, you approach it in curiosity. 
Reading it, you realize it is a small letter from Judith, seemingly made on the spot.
She is inviting you to her manor, stating that she wishes to see you. The time of the meeting is up to your decision, but she hopes you can come sometime this week. At the bottom of the letter, a lipstick residue of a kiss was made next to your name. 
You shudder, realizing that maybe Isham was right about Lady Sinclair. She is definitely dangerous…the question is whether you are into this or not?
The sound of your head banging could be heard from across the guild. 
It does not take long for Isham to knock on your door.
