<<change_background "black background">>
After paying the check, the two of you return back to the guild to finish the rest of your work that day. 
You have a hard time falling asleep that night. A mess of emotions keeps you up later than you wish, leaving you feeling dead tired by the next morning.
But work is work. No getting out of it. At the very least, your smelting job is now done. All that’s left is a handful of small tasks until it is time to choose a commission.
Thankfully, this day went by calmly. Judith did not come by again to visit. It seems she intends to wait for your visit now.
Locking the door to your forge, you decide that a pair of new gloves is in order for when you begin the shaping of the metal. It seems you will be taking another trip to the market.
<<change_background "market">>
Going through the rows of stalls in search of a proper artisan, you hear a familiar voice arguing with another. Curious, you approach the conversation where you see an injured Silas trying to bargain with a merchant of medicine. 
<<sp 4>>
With a leg wrapped in bloody bandages, the hunter struggled to stand as they haggle down the price of herbs.
However, you know for a fact that the Merchant they are up against is one famous for never backing down. Should you provide a helping hand to the prideful hunter?
<<MC true>>
-> No need to intervene. Let Silas finish their business first.
